<title>POLAND: POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 0.8 PCT IN FEB 1-10 - NBP.</title>
<headline>POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 0.8 PCT IN FEB 1-10 - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 1.11</p>
<p>billion zlotys, or 0.8 percent, in the February 1-10 period to</p>
<p>137.16 billion after a 0.1 pct rise in January, preliminary</p>
<p>central bank figures showed.</p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		     FEB 1-10   JAN 97   FEB 96</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)		0.8	  0.1	 2.5</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   137.16     136.04    108.06</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	24.29	24.26     21.29</p>
<p>  National currency		     112.86     111.79     86.77</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    23.26	22.77     20.19</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector    83.95	83.37     58.37</p>
<p>NOTE - revised figures in brackets</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
